# SPEAK-EVAL-004. Audio is opt-in, never opt-out.
#
# The failure this prevents is an accidental `git add` of a downloaded
# recording: once restricted audio is in the history, removing it means
# rewriting the history, and the licence problem has already happened.
#
# So every audio extension is ignored by default. An item that is genuinely
# cleared to live in the repo must be force-added AND declared in
# manifest.json -- validate.py sweeps this tree and fails on any audio file it
# does not recognise, which is the half of the guard that catches a file
# somebody force-added and then forgot to declare.
*.wav
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.mp4
*.webm
*.ogg
*.flac
*.opus
*.aac
artifacts/
official/
sources/
candidate_text/
scores/
variance/
